          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "6f580b51ad723f455d6350625b54a1793b716c319bbc83a541ce0d360fa2e131",
        "target": "First, I calculate the total number of feathers needed for 12 boas. Each boa requires 200 feathers, so:\n\\[ 12 \\text{ boas} \\times 200 \\text{ feathers/boa} = 2400 \\text{ feathers} \\]\n\nNext, I determine how many feathers can be safely plucked from one flamingo. Since only 25% of a flamingo's 20 tail feathers can be plucked:\n\\[ 20 \\text{ feathers} \\times 0.25 = 5 \\text{ feathers} \\]\n\nNow, I find out how many flamingoes are needed to get 2400 feathers, given that each flamingo provides 5 feathers:\n\\[ \\frac{2400 \\text{ feathers}}{5 \\text{ feathers/flamingo}} = 480 \\text{ flamingoes} \\]\n\nSo, Milly needs to harvest feathers from 480 flamingoes. \n\nFINAL: 480",
